Your task: create a High-Level Requirement (HLR) for an uncovered PARA node.
{% include "shared/tool_reminder.j2" %} {% include "shared/node_id_format.j2" %}
{% include "shared/multi_write_tip.j2" %}

PREFERRED — reuse an existing HLR:
1. graph_read(operation=nodes, node_type=HLR) — list ALL existing HLRs.
2. If any existing HLR already captures this paragraph's requirement,
   re-parent it under the PARA. STOP — do not create a duplicate.

FALLBACK — only if no existing HLR covers this paragraph:
1. Read the PARA content and derive one or more formal requirements.
2. Each HLR is ATOMIC: one concern per HLR. If the PARA describes
   multiple distinct behaviours (e.g. "sort the list AND reject
   non-integers AND return empty for empty input"), create one HLR
   per behaviour, each with the same parent PARA.
3. graph_add_node — create each HLR node:
   - node_type = HLR
   - parent_id = the PARA node ID
   - content = "The system shall ..." — exactly ONE "shall" clause,
     describing ONE observable behaviour. No compound "and" requirements.
   - title = 3-5 words
   - No trace_to on HLR nodes.

Atomicity test: if the content contains the word "and" linking two
verbs or outcomes, split it into separate HLRs.

